## 4. GKE Clusters

Two GKE Standard clusters were deployed.

### Alpha

``` text
Cluster:   enterprise-gke-alpha
Zone:      us-central1-a
Node pool: alpha-node-pool
Machine:   e2-medium
Disk:      30 GB pd-balanced
```

### Delta

``` text
Cluster:   enterprise-gke-delta
Zone:      us-east1-b
Node pool: delta-node-pool
Machine:   e2-medium
Disk:      30 GB pd-balanced
```

The normal lab topology uses two worker nodes per cluster.

Alpha was temporarily increased during troubleshooting and validation
when additional scheduling capacity was required.

Both clusters use:

-   VPC-native networking
-   Kubernetes resource requests and limits
-   multiple application replicas
-   topology spread constraints
-   Horizontal Pod Autoscaling
-   Workload Identity
-   Secret Manager integration
-   Gateway API support

Zonal clusters were selected for the lab to reduce cost. A production
design would normally consider regional GKE clusters for greater
control-plane and workload availability.

