## 11. GitHub Actions CI/CD

The Navigation application uses GitHub Actions for CI/CD.

The pipeline includes:

``` text
GitHub
   |
   v
GitHub Actions
   |
   +--> Google Workload Identity Federation
   |
   +--> Build linux/amd64 container
   |
   +--> Trivy vulnerability scan
   |
   +--> Push image to Artifact Registry
   |
   +--> Binary Authorization attestation
   |
   v
Deploy immutable image digest to GKE
```

Workload Identity Federation eliminates the need to store a Google Cloud
service-account JSON key in GitHub.

The dedicated deployment service account is:

``` text
github-actions-deployer@starfleet-gke-platform-lab.iam.gserviceaccount.com
```

The pipeline uses immutable SHA256 image digests for deployment rather
than relying only on mutable image tags.

