## 19. Multi-Cluster Failover and Failback

Cross-region failover was tested using the Navigation application.

### Normal Operation

The global frontend initially returned:

``` json
{"quadrant":"alpha","service":"starfleet-navigation-service","status":"operational"}
```

### Simulated Alpha Application Failure

The Alpha Navigation deployment was temporarily scaled to zero:

``` bash
kubectl scale deployment starfleet-navigation-service --replicas=0
```

Repeated requests to the same global frontend transitioned from Alpha to
Delta:

``` text
Global endpoint -> Alpha
Global endpoint -> Delta
Global endpoint -> Delta
Global endpoint -> Delta
```

Delta returned:

``` json
{"quadrant":"delta","service":"starfleet-navigation-service","status":"operational"}
```

### Failback

Alpha was restored:

``` bash
kubectl scale deployment starfleet-navigation-service --replicas=2
```

After Alpha became healthy, repeated requests transitioned from Delta
back to Alpha.

``` text
Global endpoint -> Delta
Global endpoint -> Alpha
Global endpoint -> Alpha
Global endpoint -> Alpha
```

### Result

``` text
Normal state:              Alpha   PASS
Alpha backend unavailable: Delta   PASS
Alpha restored:            Alpha   PASS
```

The test demonstrated application failover and failback across two GCP
regions while maintaining the same global frontend endpoint.

