## 21. Cloud DNS Decision

The Cloud DNS API is enabled.

A public Cloud DNS managed zone was intentionally **not** created
because the lab does not currently have an owned public domain available
for delegation.

Creating a Cloud DNS zone alone does not provide ownership of an
Internet domain.

The global application endpoint is therefore currently accessed through:

``` text
34.49.192.254
```

A production deployment could later configure an owned hostname with an
`A` record pointing to this static global address.

